            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention relates to an apparatus (1100) for obtaining at least one portion of a biological tissue, comprising a plurality of tubes (1010), each tube of the plurality of tubes (1010) comprising at least two points provided at a distal end thereof; a plurality of pins (1040), each pin of the plurality of pins (1040) provided at least partially within a corresponding central lumen of a respective tube of the plurality of tubes (1010). Thereby, at least one section of each tube of the plurality of tubes (1010) is structured to be inserted into the biological tissue at a donor site to remove a corresponding portion of the biological tissue therefrom when the at least one section of each tube of the plurality of tubes (1010) is withdrawn from the donor site; wherein each pin of the plurality of pins (1040) is configured to facilitate a removal of the corresponding portion of the biological tissue from the respective tube of the plurality of tubes (1040); and wherein the plurality of tubes (1040) includes a first tube and a second tube, the first tube is independently translatable from the second tube.</p>
